  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 120 PM MDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nThunderstorms not expected to be as widespread this afternoon\nand evening as last couple of days. Heat advisory will expire\nthis evening and will not continue it as Monday looks to be\ncooler a bit despite very hot still. Starting to see some\nwildfire smoke overtake western areas into Burley this afternoon\nand added in some smoke to grids through Monday. Expect a\nmoisture increase with continuing southwesterly flow aloft with\na higher chance of showers and thunderstorms Tuesday and\nWednesday mainly in higher elevations. Models indicating drying\nand warming with extreme heat back in play Thursday into next\nweekend. Low elevation highs back into the upper 90s to around\n100 again by Friday and Saturday. But overall this extremely hot\nJuly will continue through the end of the week as it will remain\nwell above normal temperature wise all the way to the end of the\nmonth.",
